            <ArticleTitle>Genetics of obstructive sleep apnea/hypopnea syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3135-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To have a better understanding of genetic contributions to the development of obstructive sleep apnea hypopnea syndrome (OSAHS) by reviewing studies on its genetic basis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DATA SOURCES" NlmCategory="METHODS">A comprehensive search of the PubMed literature without restriction on the publication date was carried out using terms &quot;obstructive sleep apnea&quot; and &quot;candidate genes&quot; or &quot;genetics&quot;.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY SELECTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Articles were selected if they were an original research paper or meta analysis of the genetic factors of OSAHS.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Four intermediate phenotypes were described and several candidate genes that may determine the expression and severity of OSAHS were reviewed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Multiple gene-gene interactions occurring in genes that affect obesity, craniofacial structure, ventilator control and asleep-awake pattern may influence the expression of OSAHS in a suitable environment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
